WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.910
Jason Blum and James Wan's new horror flick
"M3GAN" has become the "Citizen Kane" of killer

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:09.809
doll movies, notching an unexpectedly high
critics rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.759
But what are moviegoers and everyday people
actually saying about the film?

00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:20.240
Directed by Gerard Johnstone, "M3GAN" focuses
on a toy company roboticist named Gemma who

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.630
creates a life-like doll that runs on artificial
intelligence.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.029
According to the Rotten Tomatoes synopsis,

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.880
If that didn't sound creepy enough, Gemma
actually decides to give her own 8-year-old

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.010
niece the first M3GAN prototype, leading to
some horrific consequences.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:43.939
"You should probably run."

00:00:43.939 --> 00:00:49.329
Rotten Tomatoes' critical consensus describes
"M3GAN" as being "unapologetically silly and

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:54.309
all the more entertaining for it," calling
it a "rare horror-comedy that delivers chuckles

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:55.850
as effortlessly as chills."

00:00:56.104 --> 00:00:57.447
"It sounds like you're fighting."

00:00:57.447 --> 00:00:58.482
"We're not fighting!"

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:03.140
But everyone knows critics and moviegoers
can often have different opinions when it

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.080
comes to mainstream films.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.450
However, it seems that "M3GAN" is also a hit
among general moviegoers, with the film being

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.049
praised far and wide on social media.

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:13.110
One Twitter user said,

00:01:22.529 --> 00:01:23.850
Another user tweeted,

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:40.506
One user even declared, "M3GAN is a perfect
movie," while another singled out the music,

00:01:40.506 --> 00:01:41.285
posting,

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:48.691
Overall, it seems that most people who come
out of "M3GAN" are actually loving the horror

00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:51.610
flick, and not holding back their love for
it.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:56.430
The general consensus is that it's a movie
that doesn't take itself too seriously, and

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:01.120
in similar fashion, neither should audiences
— which is exactly what's happening.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.729
Going into "M3GAN," most people seem to understand
that this isn't some dramatic character study.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:07.229
As one Twitter user puts it,

00:02:19.432 --> 00:02:20.432
"Oh really?"

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.230
A "campy good time" is a common refrain.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.230
One Redditor posted,

00:02:36.201 --> 00:02:38.000
Another of the site's users wrote,

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.880
When making "M3GAN," director Gerard Johnstone
made sure to create a movie that was both

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.850
self-aware and campy, but also enjoyable and
actually good at the same time.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:02.379
He told Collider in a January 3 interview,

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:11.099
So Johnstone tried to find a happy medium,
